Z||000002||Standard||08-30-2001||10:52 PM||||Well, a suped up v6 will probably run you close to what a v8 would cost, and still not be as fast.  <P>The best options would be a v8 or a homebuilt turbo kit on a v6.  IMHO<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||08-30-2001||11:10 PM||||I would vote for series II supercharged v6, for daily driving fuel economey and getup and go.  Don't know about stick or auto, still thinking???  I think too for weight reasons a done up six would work well.  But still the sound of a sbc, ahhhhh.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forsalestart.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroMaster88||08-31-2001||02:22 AM||||Well...I put a stock V6 with a 5 speed in my car.  It was a 4 cyl auto.  I did this because the engine and trans was free!  (thanks to The Fieromaster)  All I had to pay for was a new fuel pump and a clutch line.($135 total)  It is a lot better than the 4 cyl as far as preformance!  Ooh yeah...and it only took a week to install and have working, most of that time was messin round with the darn clutch!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">            <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe With a new V6<BR>5 speed Isuzu trans<BR>AcCel 8mm wires<BR>rapid fire plugs<BR>custom intake with K&N filter.<BR>Soon to be 2" closer to the ground and have a turbo||||reg||1
